# The headend's equipment

The network runs on what **stands in the headend** - the cable provider's office. All of it is furniture from the office furniture stores (in the store or by phone):
- **CMTS DOCSIS 3.0** - the internet over the cable, up to 500 Mbit/s;
- **CMTS DOCSIS 3.1** - up to 1000 Mbit/s, then every neighbourhood's nodes are upgraded;
- **OLT** - fiber to the home (XGS-PON);
- **Satellite head-end** - the TV channels, **CA system** - encrypted Pay-TV;
- **Voice platform** - phone lines, **IPTV platform** - TV over the internet line.

Each piece costs power and maintenance every day. If the building is no longer yours or no CMTS stands there, the whole network is down.
